WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.710
- Well, you've got something
else to look forward to.

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:03.270
So I hear next year it's Walk of Fame.

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:04.103
You're getting your Walk of Fame,

00:00:04.103 --> 00:00:04.954
your star?
- Yes.

00:00:04.954 --> 00:00:06.404
(audience cheers)
Thank you.

00:00:07.274 --> 00:00:08.730
- That's so cool.
- You had yours.

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:12.000
- I literally just had, I just did mine.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.260
And you know what, I'm gonna tell you

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:14.370
the weirdest thing about it.

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:15.780
It's awesome. All of it is awesome.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:20.780
But I have never, in 20 years,
had everyone from every part

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.910
of my career under one
umbrella, like one tent,

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:25.020
for one thing.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.520
It's the first time that's ever happened.

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.230
So you're gonna look out and see people-

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:30.210
- That sounds very stressful.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.290
- You know what, it wasn't.

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:32.123
- It wasn't?

00:00:32.123 --> 00:00:34.950
- No. I tend to not keep
those people around.

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:36.240
- That's smart. That's smart.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:37.073
- Yeah.

00:00:37.073 --> 00:00:38.610
- I just am like, so I,

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.170
first of all, I don't know who to invite.

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:42.330
I'm like, am I gonna
fill the number of seats?

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:43.800
'Cause I'm like kind of a homebody.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:45.600
Second of all, like, there's
so much, there's like,

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:46.650
do you put your hands in the,

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:47.483
is that just a-

00:00:47.483 --> 00:00:48.600
- That's Grauman's.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:49.620
That's Grauman's where they do the,

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:50.453
that's a different thing.

00:00:50.453 --> 00:00:52.410
It's right there, like,
where the stars are.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:54.030
But it's a, I learned this.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:55.350
- Wait, there's two different ways-

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:56.183
- Exactly.

00:00:56.183 --> 00:00:58.110
- That we commemorate famous people?

00:00:58.110 --> 00:01:00.300
- Exactly. We come up with them.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:01.320
I didn't know this either.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:02.557
And so whenever it was
happening I was like,

00:01:02.557 --> 00:01:03.450
"Do I have to do my hands or something?"

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:04.390
They're like, "No, it's Grauman's."

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:06.390
- Wait, I'm here getting all like,

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:08.850
excited to do that photo where I'm on-

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:10.590
- Well, you do the photo where you're on

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:12.150
the ground with the star.

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:14.678
Which try and look attractive
in that environment.

00:01:14.678 --> 00:01:15.777
(Mindy laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:01:15.777 --> 00:01:17.100
I literally saw the
pictures and I was like,

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.120
I guess approve.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.470
Like, they're horrible.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:21.600
But like, it's just like the most awkward-

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:24.810
- You have to lay down
sideways on the dirty street.

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:27.060
- Yeah. It's not great.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:30.360
That look isn't great, but
I'm sure you'll pull it off.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.330
I didn't and I just leaned into humor.

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:35.220
But will your "Office" co-stars be there?

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:36.894
Will people that you've been
working with, are you gonna-

00:01:36.894 --> 00:01:38.880
- I'll invite them. I'll invite
them. They're pretty busy.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:40.770
I think there's a couple
that'll definitely,

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:41.970
definitely come.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:43.290
I think it'll be fun.

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:46.290
I'm one of these people,
I don't like to ever,

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:50.790
I mean I try to, but I have
trouble reflecting on success

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:53.460
'cause I'm superstitious and
I feel like if you spend too

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:56.370
much time thinking about
like, oh, you did a great job

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:57.690
or you should commemorate this,

00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:59.160
that something bad is gonna happen.

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.500
It's like, I don't know. I'm
just like, one of those people.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:04.500
So sometimes big life milestones,

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.940
like I didn't do a baby shower,

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:07.710
I didn't do any of that
stuff 'cause I was like,

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:09.030
I don't wanna jinx something.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.980
I've just always been this way.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.050
- [Kelly] Oh, I'm so opposite of you.

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:14.940
- Well, listen, that's
the healthy way to be.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:16.110
- I didn't actually want a baby shower

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:17.850
because I hated pregnancy
and I just wanted

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:19.350
all humans to get away from me.

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:21.630
But like, but most times I think it's,

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:23.010
I think try and think of it though,

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:25.290
it's also kind of cool to go,

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:27.210
I think because in my career,

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:28.170
I don't know if you feel the same,

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:29.580
you forget things that happen.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:31.320
- Yeah.
- Like you forget because you

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.450
didn't take the time to have that moment.

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:35.040
You didn't take the time to have that-

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:36.840
- To commemorate it.
- Commemorate it, yeah.

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:37.890
Yeah. So I don't know.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:39.930
But what the hell do I know?

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:42.120
- To my kids, I can be like,
"See, I'm like a big deal.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.050
Don't give me any crap."

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:44.190
- No, I'm telling you my six

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:45.240
and eight year old were
there and they were like,

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:47.070
they literally leaned over
to my mom and my sister,

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:48.736
I can't remember which one
it was, and they were like,

00:02:48.736 --> 00:02:51.720
"Why is everybody like
yelling, like for my mom?"

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:54.120
They were like, they just
thought it was so weird.

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:55.650
So it's kind of cool to see.

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.630
You're like, yeah, mommy works hard.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:00.160
I was like, it's kind nice
to be like, "That's right."

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:01.887
- No, it's true.
- [Kelly] It's nice.

